# Questions and answers. Updated for the final deck (22 to 24 November 2026): 912 tests, five games, demo checkout.
# Each answer is meant to be SAID in about 20 to 40 seconds. Shape for anything unexpected:
#   (1) what we did, (2) what the data or source shows, (3) what we did not measure, (4) what we would do next.

HOW_TO = [
 "Cover the answer, say your own answer out loud, then compare. **Do not memorize the wording; learn the shape.**",
 "The shape for any question you did not expect: **(1) what we did, (2) what the data or the source shows, (3) what we did not measure, (4) what we would do next.**",
 "**FILL** means the real number or sentence must come from your own appendices or your own team. Do not invent it. **CHECK** means look at the source before you say it.",
 "If you do not know: \"I will check the appendix and come back to you.\" A panel respects that far more than a guess.",
]

